## 🔒 Security Considerations

### Development vs Production

**Development (This Example):**
- Uses mock wallet for demonstration
- No real private keys exposed
- Safe for testing and development

**Production Integration:**
- Use real wallet adapters (Freighter, WalletConnect, etc.)
- Never expose private keys
- Implement proper error handling
- Add transaction validation

### Best Practices

```tsx
// ✅ Good: Production-ready error handling
<PayWithUSDC
  amount={amount}
  destination={destination}
  wallet={realWallet}
  onSuccess={(hash) => {
    // Log success for analytics
    analytics.track('payment_success', { hash, amount });
    // Update UI state
    setPaymentStatus('completed');
  }}
  onError={(error) => {
    // Log error for debugging
    console.error('Payment failed:', error);
    // Show user-friendly message
    setErrorMessage('Payment failed. Please try again.');
  }}
/>

// ❌ Bad: Exposing private keys
const badWallet = {
  getPublicKey: () => "G...",
  signAndSubmit: async (xdr) => {
    // NEVER do this in production!
    const secret = "S...PRIVATE_KEY";
    return signAndSubmit(xdr, secret);
  }
};
```

